{
  "case_id": "2016-16-349",
  "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent's only answer to this is to say that this -- no, no, this is a provision that is addressed at the bank that is simply holding the debts as collateral. But that can't be right, because at the very beginning of (F)(iv) -- or (F) -- and Congress made clear that the exception only applies to somebody who is actually collecting or attempting to collect a debt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Russell, do you have a few examples -- I -- I suspect you've thought of this -- just of sentences which use the word \"owed\" to -- to mean what you want it to mean in this case, without any other context clues?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Where -- where do they say that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In that circumstance, Santander certainly could be said to have obtained rights in the debt. But the debt is still owed or due Sam's Cars in the relevant sense. It's still owed or due Sam's Cars because in that circumstance, the creditor retains an interest in the accounts, it retains the right to demand payments on those accounts as well."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Santander",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the words have a subtly different meaning because, as we explain in a footnote of our brief, it is possible to talk about a debt being owed, but not yet due."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Shanmugam, it doesn't make much sense, though, does it? I mean, take this very case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Santander",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The relevant inquiry is whether we were a debt collector at the time of the alleged violation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Santander",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because if you take a look at page 49 of Petitioner's brief, they argue that we would fall within the assignee exclusion, which refers to a -- a person who receives an assignment or transfer of a debt in default, solely for the purpose of facilitating collection of such debt for another."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Santander",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Those violations are alleged to have taken place five years ago, and I can represent to this Court that Santander's business was, in some respects, very different. And in particular, Santander had much less servicing activity in 2012 than it does today."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But wouldn't we, assuming we agree with you, have to leave open that -- the question of the character of the business, the sixth definition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Counsel",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0003-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Their proposed solution to (F)(iv) simply doesn't work. And nobody has been able to come up with a circumstance in which (F)(iv) has any work to do or makes any coherent sense on Respondent's definition of owed or due another."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It allows, as I discussed with Justice Alito, a third-party debt collector to evade the statutes so long as it is hired to collect the debt before the debt goes into default, even once it's delinquent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-349",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "188cd69e39a2fa1f6dcd22ec0b15391758755818d32eb9b31ae6449e6da85cd5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-188cd69e39a2-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
